  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SHOREBIRS CONS PLN I</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">An effective strategy for flyway-scale conservation of long-distance migrant shorebirds must integrate international cooperation, conservation interventions, and monitoring across the full suite of geographic, ecological, and cultural landscapes. Although there are numerous shorebird conservation plans in place within the Pacific Flyway, these plans cover various geographies and there is no comprehensive, integrated full life- cycle plan for a representative suite of migrants. This project is for Phase I of a two-year project to develop a Pacific Americas Flyway Shorebird Conservation Business Plan. In Phase I, partners will convene an international planning committee to develop and refine a conceptual model with input from key stakeholders in Central and South America, Mexico, the United States and Canada. This project will help conserve many bird species, including snowy plover, red knot, hudsonian godwit and marbled godwit...</narrative>
  </description>
